  "solution": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8804;</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Putting&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>y</mi></math>&nbsp;and simplifying, we get&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />The region in shown shaded right side of the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><br /><br /><img src=\"assets\\st0176_e1a5a9513fa2.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 227px;\" /><br />The largest value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math> would be the length of perpendicular from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, on the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mfrac><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;"
  }
